# The API Dockerfile's builder stage does `COPY . .`, so without this an
# .env sitting in the working tree is copied into a build layer along with
# real Clerk and Plaid credentials. The final image does not carry it, but a
# layer that does is still a layer that can be pushed or inspected.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template

# Never belongs in an image, and makes the build context far larger than the
# source it is meant to carry.
.git
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
apps/web/.vite
.turbo

# Local agent and operator state
AGENTS.md
memory/
MEMORY.md
backups/

# Test and build output
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright-mcp/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
ml-venv/
